# One chat, one board task

The person asks to look at a task on the GitHub board. Stay in this chat. Do not suggest a new chat and do not start an autonomous loop from files in `prompts/`.

1. Read `.cursor/agents/initializer.md` and the `board-task` skill. On a new chat, first finish a merged card that is still open (step 5) and update `main` (step 6). When one task is taken, set its Status on the project `harness for gem-puzzle` to `Todo`. Bring back a description and a plan. Stop and wait.
2. After approval or edits, the evaluator moves that issue to `board:in-progress` and sets Status `In progress` on that project. Then follow `.cursor/agents/coder.md` and the coder skills in this same chat.
3. Then follow `.cursor/agents/evaluator.md` and the `verify-task` skill in this same chat. If the check fails, the coder fixes that same task here. Leave the card on `In progress`.
4. When the check passes, the evaluator follows the `keep-changelog` skill and makes one commit on the task branch. That commit contains the task changes and `CHANGELOG.md`. Then it moves the card to `board:in-review` and Status `In review` on that same project, and opens the pull request. Stop there. The person reviews the pull request and merges it. Do not merge. Do not make a second commit for the documentation or for the pull request number. Leave `CHANGELOG.md` as that skill requires.

5. After that merge, the evaluator sets `board:done` and Status `Done` on that same project and closes the issue. Leave `CHANGELOG.md` as the `keep-changelog` skill requires. Do not do the board close while the pull request is still open. If the person already left the chat, the next chat does this step before it starts the new task.

6. A new chat for a new task starts on `main`. Check out `main`, fetch, and see whether the latest merged pull request (the finished GP) is already in local `main`. If it is, follow the plan for the new GP. If it is not, pull `main` first, then follow the plan. The new branch is cut from that updated `main`.

`TASK.md` is the product description. Take technical constraints from the agent skills. Do not add them to `TASK.md`.
